00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:01.680
You'll hear my sad story?!

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:04.220
Thank you so much!

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:08.890
Let me introduce myself;
I'm Mister Leprechaun.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:11.730
I once lived in a lovely shoe, until...

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:18.360
...a passing Hero
crushed it with his foot.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.450
Then threw it over his shoulder.

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:22.660
Ew, what's with this gross shoe?

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:25.370
Then it floated down the river...

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:31.540
How can this world be so cruel?!

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:36.300
My friend and I split up to find
a new home, but it's slow goin'...

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:41.180
What? You'll help us?!

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:45.310
Your father's looking for a home, too?

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:50.190
And he's a dragon? Why would
a dragon need to look for a home?

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:55.480
Huh? It's one part of his plan
for world domination?

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:56.900
It is not!

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:05.120
Now I've got me a place to sleep.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:09.660
Now, where did my friend run off to?

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:14.540
Hey! Where are ya?

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:18.170
There he is! Ho, there!

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:22.840
It's gonna eat us!

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:24.850
The two leprechauns were reunited.

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:28.350
Forgive me for losing my composure there.

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:34.730
If you could help us find a nice,
old shoe to live in, we'd appreciate it.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:38.820
Leather if you can.
It's easy to work with.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.410
Ugh, my feet hurt.

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:46.950
Why're you makin' us scout out this place,
anyway? There's nothing here.

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:50.250
There could be a cave
or treasure hidden around here!

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:54.630
That one?!

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:56.130
We couldn't!

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:59.760
Those Heroes would have
our hides if we stole from them!

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:02.510
You're sure it'll be fine?!

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:04.640
How do you know?!

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:06.600
Dammit, get us out of here!

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:16.770
The Heroes <i>always </i>get screwed
when they show up? If you say so...

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:21.110
It's so annoying that we have to get
up close to NPCs to talk to them.

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:22.900
Wish we could interact with them
from a little further a--

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:31.040
--Bugs?!
--Eek!
--Run away! Run away!

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.330
Piyobert learned

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.330
'Caterpillar Rain'!

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:35.540
I left my shoe back there!

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:36.960
Go get it later!

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:39.250
I ain't goin' back!

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:42.460
Thank you so much.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:45.220
We've got a home, all thanks to you!

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:57.980
Thank you for all your help,
too, little fellas.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:00.320
You guys owe us one.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:00.390
You guys owe us one

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:04.110
Didja see the looks
on their faces? Classic.

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:04.190
Didja see the looks on their faces? Classic

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:10.870
Pip!

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:12.290
Papa!

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:16.210
You have to go?

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:20.090
I see. I wish we could thank you somehow.

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:26.130
Take care!

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:32.930
Pip! Pip!

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:37.390
Pip...

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:39.980
Calm down, Letty.

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:41.270
Pip...

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:45.070
Papa!

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:50.490
Papa!

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:55.620
Papa!

00:07:59.710 --> 00:08:03.460
I was so worried!

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:05.710
Pip!

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:11.390
I was so scared when I woke up
and he were gone!

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:15.140
I can't believe you let him
go off on his own like that!

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:17.270
If he's big enough
to handle himself like this,

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:20.650
he's big enough to start using his own
magic to regulate his temperature.

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:22.690
You don't need to keep him cool anymore.

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:24.480
That's not the point.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:29.660
What if he'd gotten hurt,
or someone attacked him?

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:32.700
There are no bears
or wolves in these woods.

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:35.040
At worst, there are foxes and martens.

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:36.120
Drool.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:38.120
They could eat him, too!

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:43.210
I think Pip needs to be a little bigger
before he can go on his own adventures!

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:46.800
You're quite overprotective, Letty.

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:49.010
When I was a child,

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:52.430
I lived in a snowy mountain range
where rabid berserkers roamed.

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:54.220
This is much safer, comparatively.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:58.140
Your baseline for "dangerous"
is <i>way </i>out there!

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:00.190
What were you doing out there?

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:04.060
I apprenticed with
a master that lived there.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:06.400
Wait, Dearia,

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:08.280
you had a childhood?

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:11.530
Did you think I just
spawned into existence?

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:15.450
Where do Elves come from, anyway?

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:20.790
Most of us live near in a hidden village
in the branches of Yggdrasil.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:24.960
They apparently lived in splendor
on the surface until not too long ago.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:27.460
Wow, how long ago is that?

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:29.050
About 100,000 years ago.

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:30.590
That's "not too long ago"?!

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:33.340
However, as the younger races
began to prosper,

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:35.300
the elves found themselves unsure
of how to approach them,

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:37.680
so they decided it was best
to withdraw from the mortal world.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:40.480
So elves are just socially awkward?!

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:43.520
Wow, though, an itty-bitty Dearia...

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:46.360
Would you care to explain that giddy grin?

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:49.990
Just wondering what you
were like when you little!

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:53.610
I don't have any amusing
childhood tales, sadly.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:05.580
I do have <i>one </i>tale from
a little over 1,000 years ago.

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:16.970
In the village of the elves,

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:20.220
there once lived a child who possessed
an unrivaled thirst for knowledge.

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:46.920
When I was a child, I was desperate
to absorb any knowledge I could,

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:50.920
spending most of my days
between the pages of a book.

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:54.840
Once, I tried to make a place
where I could read alone in peace.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:05.770
"Chnarb sit edisni kun
kub eezok a etaerc."

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:11.530
I failed spectacularly.

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:16.360
Dearia!

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:23.540
Why is it always you?

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:29.040
Do you not understand the ramifications
of breaking a branch of the world tree?!

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:30.250
Sorry.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:36.050
Every branch of the tree
is a manifestation of life itself!

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:37.720
I'll do better next time.

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:39.760
You're going to strip Yggdrasil bare!

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:41.430
I'll try a different spell next time.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:43.430
No, you will not!

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:48.270
I've told you again and again,

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:52.360
children must stay in the nursery.

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:55.150
You will be allowed private quarters
only when you come of age.

00:11:55.150 --> 00:12:01.120
Besides, isn't it much more fun
living together with your friends?

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:03.040
What a troublemaker.

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:09.170
I prefer to be alone.

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:16.420
There's so much I want to learn.

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:22.140
I need a place where I can read
all day without being bothered.

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:26.520
If you'd like to learn something,
then ask an adult to teach you!

00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:28.440
You shouldn't isolate yourself.

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:36.440
Says the adults who've isolated
themselves in the world tree.

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:40.490
What could you possibly know
that's not in these books?

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:42.570
You little...

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:47.540
If you are that thirsty for knowledge,

00:12:47.540 --> 00:12:50.920
then we can entrust your care
to the great wise serpent.

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:54.590
You're going to exile me because
I'm too much of a handful?

00:12:54.590 --> 00:12:57.550
It's study abroad! Study abroad!

00:12:57.550 --> 00:13:00.590
In the northernmost lands,
far, far away from here,

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:03.300
near the frozen Ergot sea,

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:08.520
lives a giant serpent who was old and wise
even when Yggdrasil first sprouted.

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:12.440
Though living in their domain
is quite dangerous,

00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:15.400
it would quench your thirst for knowledge.

00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:37.130
Welcome to the far reaches
of the north, little traveler.

00:13:37.130 --> 00:13:39.590
I have been expecting you.

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:43.180
I am Jormungandr.

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:46.510
My name is Dearia.

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:48.560
I was told that you,
who can see for 1,000 leagues,

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:52.440
could teach me everything I wish to know.

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:55.060
What is it you wish to know?

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:59.030
Are goblin loincloths
made from wool or hemp?

00:13:59.030 --> 00:14:00.400
Oh, dear!

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:05.820
That's quite the niche interest.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:08.620
It has been centuries since
anything has surprised me so.

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:10.290
I couldn't find the answer
in any of my books.

00:14:10.290 --> 00:14:13.000
Likely because no one cared enough
to preserve that knowledge.

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:24.380
Before I answer your questions,
you will need a place to build a fire.

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:29.310
No doubt there are many things
you wish to know,

00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:35.940
but there is much more you can learn
to attain the knowledge you seek.

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:42.240
Everything that exists
in our world is interconnected.

00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:49.830
An empty answer is hardly equal
to true understanding.

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:54.330
Fortunately, both you and I
are long-lived.

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:58.540
First, let us get you warmed up
so you don't go catching a cold on me.

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:03.260
After that, let us unravel
all the queries you may have.

00:15:06.930 --> 00:15:10.760
I look forward to your tutelage,

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:12.980
Master.

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:17.650
And so, I applied myself to my studies
under the tutelage of the great serpent.

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:21.190
I learned languages,
philosophy, religion, history,

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:27.030
biology, geography, astronomy,
medicine, and last but not least, magic.

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:31.330
The days I spent there
were most fulfilling.

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:33.620
There was, however, one problem.

00:15:36.710 --> 00:15:39.330
Not again.

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:42.500
Whatever is the matter, boy?

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:45.260
An earthquake flattened
my house again, Master.

00:15:45.260 --> 00:15:50.140
An earthquake?
I don't recall sensing one...

00:15:53.310 --> 00:15:55.810
Because my Master
most certainly caused it.

00:15:55.810 --> 00:15:57.230
Whoa.

00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:01.520
You're going to live there?!

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:02.570
Here, live in this house.

00:16:02.570 --> 00:16:05.690
The grown-up elves built me a house,

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:07.490
but it only lasted ten days.

00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:11.030
My Master asked some golems
to build me a house...

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:12.580
All done!

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:15.200
But that didn't even last two days.

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:19.330
If I rebuild it again, it'll likely
just collapse once more.

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:21.040
In that case...

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:24.630
Master, please resurrect me
every morning from here on out.

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:27.800
Why? Do you intend to freeze
to death every night?

00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:30.090
Temperature is not the only
threat to your life here.

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:34.970
Whatever will you do if a wandering
berserker comes upon you?

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:41.440
If I cannot ensure your safety, then I
will have to send you back to Yggdrasil.

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:45.150
I-I'll rebuild it at once!

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:47.240
This time, it'll be able
to withstand any earthquake!

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:52.240
I fear that construction is one area
in which I lack knowledge.

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:55.950
I'm sure if we put our heads together,
we can make something work!

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:59.540
I see. Very well.

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:06.260
I've heard that adding more walls
adds to a structure's strength.

00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:08.760
Why not try a denser layout?

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:10.680
It looks like a box of chocolates.

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:14.470
I don't need that many rooms, anyway.

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:16.720
Let's just give it a try.

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:19.940
Good. I'll call the golems
to help once more.

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:27.320
It's gone from a studio apartment
to having a bedroom and a kitchen.

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:29.110
Three
Days
Later

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:32.360
It didn't last, I see.

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:38.750
What if we reinforced it
with metal girders?

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:40.250
That's a fine idea.

00:17:41.920 --> 00:17:45.880
Good! Now my house will be way stronger!

00:17:54.890 --> 00:17:58.180
Cold temperatures cause metal
to stick or grow brittle.

00:17:58.180 --> 00:18:00.980
Pondering this design is somewhat fun.

00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:03.810
There's so much to learn in all of this.

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:03.890
Metal Girders: freeze,
 weak in low temps

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:08.780
Despite encountering a bit of trouble
during the design process,

00:18:08.780 --> 00:18:15.160
I was able to find a metal alloy that
would resist these cold temperatures.

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:16.740
It's finally done!

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:23.000
Master, look! I built my house!

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:24.790
Come, see it for yourself!

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:27.250
Now I can get back to studying!

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:38.970
You called for me, boy?

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:48.690
What have I done?!

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:53.950
My most deepest apologies, boy!
I am so sorry!

00:18:53.950 --> 00:18:57.870
Could those other "earthquakes"
have been my doing, too?!

00:18:57.870 --> 00:19:01.040
Doesn't seem to be going well, hmm?

00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:04.290
The materials we provided ya
were no match for her.

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:06.500
Well, of course not.

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:10.000
She's never been good about
watchin' out for her tail.

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:12.510
The Graiae sisters...

00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:14.550
Now, cheer up there, Dear Boy.

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:16.180
No helpin' it around her.

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:19.970
Hard for such a little guy to live
'round a ginormous serpent.

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:23.430
At least you didn't end up
crushed to death inside it!

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:26.940
Might be safer for ya
if you ran along home.

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:31.650
No. I will stay here.

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:33.240
Why?

00:19:33.240 --> 00:19:35.070
What, back already?

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:37.610
Done with your studies already?

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:41.620
If I went back to the world tree,
the adults would just sneer at me.

00:19:41.620 --> 00:19:42.660
What's wrong with them?

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:44.040
How childish.

00:19:44.040 --> 00:19:46.080
What a pain.

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:47.120
Not only that...

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:50.210
If I can design a building that
can withstand Jormungandr,

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:57.130
Price
Negotiable

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:51.750
then I'll make boatloads of money.

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:53.840
In it for the money, huh?

00:19:53.840 --> 00:19:55.260
That's our little entrepreneur.

00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:57.380
Let us invest in ya, yeah?

00:20:03.020 --> 00:20:06.600
Despite everything,

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:10.440
I want to stay here with you, Master.

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:13.690
Dearia...

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:20.870
Aww, us old grannies'll
give ya a helpin' hand.

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:27.290
Go on, take whatever you want!

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:34.050
How sturdy is this lumber?

00:20:34.050 --> 00:20:36.550
That's silver willow.

00:20:36.550 --> 00:20:39.590
It's light and sturdy,

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:42.970
but it won't hold up to Jormungandr.

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:56.740
Whaddya say, boy? Think it'll work?

00:20:56.740 --> 00:20:57.860
Yes, it will.

00:20:57.860 --> 00:21:01.410
I'm finished!

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:12.420
Well, earthquakes certainly won't
affect it up here, nor can I crush it.

00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:14.550
Good thinking.

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:18.840
Of course it was.

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:22.260
I learned from the best, Master!

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:25.470
That you did, boy.

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:29.100
I have myself a fine apprentice.

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:31.690
One question, Master.

00:21:31.690 --> 00:21:34.270
What should I do when nature calls?

00:21:34.270 --> 00:21:37.860
Wh-Wha...?!

00:21:37.860 --> 00:21:39.990
Time passed.

00:21:41.320 --> 00:21:45.450
I spent a few centuries
as Dark Lord in name only.

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:50.960
Just when mankind had forgotten
about the Dark Lord altogether...

00:21:57.500 --> 00:22:01.130
That is when <i>he </i>came calling.

00:23:32.390 --> 00:23:32.970
Elf Housing Realty

00:23:32.970 --> 00:23:33.010
Elf Housing Realty

00:23:33.010 --> 00:23:33.050
Elf Housing Realty

00:23:33.350 --> 00:23:34.890
Do you like insects?

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:37.690
If you don't, have you considered
changing the lighting in your home?

00:23:37.690 --> 00:23:41.360
Fluorescent lights emit UV radiation
that attracts insects.

00:23:37.850 --> 00:23:41.390
Fluorescent Lighting

00:23:41.360 --> 00:23:45.110
LED lightbulbs can solve
that insect problem for you.

00:23:41.390 --> 00:23:43.770
Fluorescent Lighting

00:23:45.110 --> 00:23:47.410
Next time, "A Home for a Black Dragon."

00:23:47.650 --> 00:23:47.690
Elf Housing Realty

00:23:47.690 --> 00:23:47.730
Elf Housing Realty

00:23:47.730 --> 00:23:48.400
Elf Housing Realty
